(11635,33,'_edit_last','1'),
(11636,33,'_quills_hero_title','About Us'),
(11637,33,'_quills_where_we_started_title','WHERE WE STARTED'),
(11638,33,'_quills_where_we_started_paragraphs','a:10:{i:0;s:111:\"In the early 2000s, many people drank coffee without thinking much about it. I couldn\'t stop thinking about it.\";i:1;s:156:\"During my time as a social worker, I was meeting with students in local coffeehouses. I found myself constantly talking about what makes exceptional coffee.\";i:2;s:75:\"How it\'s sourced, roasted, how it\'s brewed. And why doing it right matters.\";i:3;s:117:\"In 2007, we took a pair of hammers to an old rundown building in the Germantown neighborhood of Louisville, Kentucky.\";i:4;s:188:\"After a lot of love and elbow grease, we opened the first Quills. That first shop taught us everything. We learned that great coffee can create the kind of spaces where people can connect.\";i:5;s:150:\"We learned that when you blend fine coffee with a touch of southern hospitality, when you prioritize connection over speed, something special happens.\";i:6;s:211:\"You make places where strangers can become friends. Where a writer finds her words in a warm corner seat. Where a company might be founded on the back of a napkin. Where first dates can turn into something more.\";i:7;s:187:\"When our first building was about to be sold and we had to move, our regular customer Tommy O\'Shea helped us find a new home in the Highlands. That shop on Baxter Avenue runs to this day.\";i:8;s:335:\"We\'ve grown since then. Today, we roast our coffee in small batches right here in Louisville. Because we wanted better control over the whole experience we were creating. Today we have six cafes here and one in downtown Indianapolis. But at the heart of it all, the vision hasn\'t changed: Great coffee. Great spaces. Great hospitality.\";i:9;s:247:\"We work with our producers and sourcing partners around the world who care deeply about quality. The close work we do with them means that every cup you drink is connected to real people, real farms, and a commitment to doing things the right way.\";}'),
(11639,33,'_quills_why_were_here_title','WHY WE\'RE HERE'),
(11640,33,'_quills_why_were_here_content','Quills Coffee is here to deliver a coffee that connects people. Between the barista behind the counter and the customer in front of it. Between strangers at neighboring tables. Between all of us and the farmers who picked the coffee we\'re enjoying. We believe delivering great coffee is a chance to make memorable human experiences. It\'s a chance for us to be together, to pause, to talk, to connect.'),
(11641,33,'_quills_how_we_work_title','HOW WE WORK'),
(11642,33,'_quills_how_we_work_content','The French have a word: terroir. It means \"the taste of the place itself.\" The soil where something grows. The climate that shapes it. The hands that tend it. It\'s why a coffee cherry from Guatemala tastes different from one grown in Ethiopia. The earth was different, the rain was different, and so the taste is different. At Quills, we celebrate our own kind of \"terroir\" with three core values: Genuine Care, Continuous Craft, and Creative Education.'),
(11643,33,'_quills_where_were_going_quote','Like soil worked for years, our roots merely grow richer with time. We\'re not trying to be the biggest coffee company, or the fastest. We\'re building a place where quality lives, where every cup honors the taste of each dear sight, and most importantly—where people strive to connect with other people.'),
(11644,33,'_quills_where_were_going_author','— Nathan Quillo, Founder'),
